--- Finding (arithmetic_evaluation): a record answered by a call that can fail (a
--- function answering a record or an error value), handed to a function whose
--- parameter is a record or none (the function also hands itself node.left), does
--- not build compiled: the call's payload is passed bare where the parameter
--- takes a link.
---
--- crow run -i:  prints 2
--- crow run:     error[E0308]: mismatched types --> src/main.rs
---                 depth(&_prop_0.value): expected `&Option<Arc<Node>>`, found `&Node`
---               error: the compiled program does not build — the Rust compiler refused
---               what Crow accepted, a bug in Crow, not in this program
--- Expected: 2 in both modes.
--- The same record built in place, depth[Node[Node[0]]], builds (it is wrapped as
--- Some(link::new(...))). Guarding first (tree = make[1], then `if not tree.ok` /
--- `return …`, then depth[tree]) does not build either. Seen in a parser whose
--- parse[text] answers a tree or an error, and whose evaluate and shown walk the
--- tree by node.left and node.right.
struct Node [left]

fn depth[node]
    if node eq 0
        return 0
    return 1 + depth[node.left]

fn make[n]
    if n lt 0
        return error['negative']
    return Node[Node[0]]

log[depth[make[1]]]
